  "narrative": {
    "intro": "The 8(a) Business Development set-aside program recorded $57.2M in obligations in FY2027 to date. The program produced 238 awards with an average award size of $240K, and obligations were down 99.4% year over year. Fiscal-year obligations for recent years show much larger totals: FY22 recorded $12.2B, FY23 recorded $14.1B, FY24 recorded $15.1B, FY25 recorded $13.7B, and FY26 recorded $10.1B. The FY2027 to date total of $57.2M sits well below those prior fiscal-year totals. The Department of Homeland Security obligated $27M in FY2027 to date, the Department of Health and Human Services obligated $9.5M, and the Department of the Treasury obligated $5.7M. Computer Systems Design Services accounted for $16.5M of obligations, and Facilities Support Services accounted for $11.4M. KONIAG BRILLIENT, LLC received $11.4M, CAS FSE JV II LLC received $8.9M, and INTUITIVE INFORMATION SYSTEMS TECHNOLOGIES LLC received $7.2M in FY2027 to date.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Why are FY2027 to-date obligations so low compared with prior years?",
        "body": "Obligations fell 99.4% year over year in FY2027 to date. Fiscal-year totals for FY22 through FY26 were $12.2B, $14.1B, $15.1B, $13.7B, and $10.1B respectively, while FY27 to date is $57.2M. The award count in FY2027 to date is 238 with an average award size of $240K."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which agencies and industries dominate FY2027 8(a) obligations?",
        "body": "The Department of Homeland Security is the top buyer in FY2027 to date, obligating $27M. The Department of Health and Human Services obligated $9.5M and the Department of the Treasury obligated $5.7M. Computer Systems Design Services leads industries with $16.5M and Facilities Support Services follows with $11.4M."
      }
    ]
  },
